Planned data sources (attribution recorded ahead of bundling)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The spherical-Earth epic (#468) integrates several open geospatial datasets. Each
carries its own attribution obligation, recorded here so the requirement is in
place BEFORE the data is bundled. When the corresponding data is added to a
release, its attribution must also be surfaced to players in-game.

ESA WorldCover — land-cover classification (terrain biomes, #475)
  Source:   © ESA WorldCover project / Contains modified Copernicus data.
  License:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
            *** Attribution is REQUIRED when this data is distributed. ***
  URL:      https://esa-worldcover.org/

Copernicus Sentinel-2 — high-resolution satellite terrain textures (#488)
  Source:   Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data.
  License:  Copernicus data terms (free, full, open access; attribution required).
  URL:      https://sentinel.esa.int/

GEBCO — global ocean bathymetry (#476)
  Source:   GEBCO Compilation Group.
  License:  GEBCO Grid terms (freely available; attribution requested).
  URL:      https://www.gebco.net/

OurAirports — airport / runway registry (#486)
  Source:   OurAirports (David Megginson and contributors).
  License:  Public domain.
  URL:      https://ourairports.com/data/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In-game credits
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every bundled data source that requires attribution (notably the CC BY 4.0 ESA
WorldCover data) must be credited on a player-reachable credits surface in the
game before that data ships in a release. The only data bundled today (WMM2025)
is public domain and imposes no such requirement; the in-game credits surface is
added together with the first attribution-bearing dataset it must display.
